tion  which of the following are the types of  constructors in kotlin  so first is parameterized and constant  constructor  option b is primary constructor and  secondary constructor option c is  default and no argument constructor and  option d is none of the above so you can  take your time in figuring out the  correct option among these four options  because i am going to say its correct  option you can pause the video and take  your time  so our correct option is option b  primary constructor and secondary  constructor are the types of constructor  in kotlin  so option b is the correct option  now moving on to our next question that  is the fifth question which is  how to get the length of the string in  kotlin  so this is also a multiple choice  question  our options are a  str.length of  option b length str  option c  str.length and option d  str dot length off with small o  so you can take your time in figuring  out what is the correct option  meanwhile  i'm gonna say the correct option  so a right or correct option is  option c  str.length  so if you want to  get the length of a string in kotlin you  can use str.length  now  moving on to the next question which is  which feature allows  removing the risk of occurrence of null  pointer exception  so it is an important question as well  so  there are four options first null risk b  null safety c null pointer and d all of  the above  it is a very important question  and  now the correct option of this question  is  e null safety  null safety allows us to remove the risk  of occurrence of null pointer exception  it is a very essential feature of kotlin  language  now  moving on to the seventh question which  is  what is null safety and nullable types  in kotlin  so null safety commonly referred to as  void safety ensures that no object  references have null or void values  whereas in kotlin nullable types are  references types that are declared by  appending a question mark to the string  this question mark is what we add at the  end of the data type to make it as  nullable  now moving on to the eighth question  which is  what is higher order function in kotlin  a higher order function accepts one or  more function as arguments and returns a  function as output  it is not like any other function  the higher order functions are  frequently combined with lambda  expression to create code that is both  compact and powerful  instead of integer string or array as a  parameter to the function  we will pass anonymous function or  lambdas in higher order function  so basically we pass a function to other  function known as higher order function  now  moving on to the ninth question which is  what is elvis operator  the null safety attribute in kotlin  allows us to assign null values to the  variables  can use if else or the always operator  to see if a value has a null value  always operator returns the first  operand and if that operand is true  otherwise evaluates and returns the  other operand  now our next question is  why is scotland interoperable with java  so this is our tenth question  so kotlin is compatible with java  because it uses jvm bytecode  jetbrains places a strong emphasis on  kotlin's interaction with existing java  code while building compatibility  the team ensures that kotlin can  interface with existing java code easily  and thoroughly  compiling it directly to bytecode speeds  up the compilation process and  eliminates the distinction between java  and kotlin on jvm  so this is the reason kotlin is  interoperable with java  now coming on to the 11th question which  is  what are the range expressions  a range is a set of values defined by  their beginning and ending points  range expression in kotlin make it  easier to iterate over a set of values  to make a range in kotlin use the range  2 and down 2 functions  we may also define a range of values by  using the double dots operator  as we can see in the example for i in 1  double dot 10  this will print all the elements from 1  to 10  and for 10 in  down to 1 will print all the elements  from 10 to 1.  in descending order  the third one is which is  4  i in 1 double dot 10 step 2  this will print  elements with a gap  now step two means there's a gap  so it will print elements like one  three  five seven nine because we have used  step two if we use step three then it  will give a gap of two  like 1  4 like that so on  moving on to the 12th question which is  what do you understand by data class  so data classes are the classes that are  used to hold the data or information  these data classes were previously  exclusively used to generate java codes  but with the explicit implementation of  the higher and greater collection of  properties they are now important in  kotlin as well  functions like tostring and equals are  also combined with this language  now moving on to the 13th question which  is immutable variable  so this is a multiple choice question  and the options are a variable that are  change that can be changed b a variable  that cannot change that is read only  c a variable used for string  interpolation  d none of the above  so  we have already talked about immutable  variable  and  you can pick the correct option  now i am going to say the correct option  so the correct option is b a variable  that cannot be changed is called  immutable variable that is the variable  that cannot be changed  now  coming on to the 14th question which is  what are co routines it is a very  important concept  so the letters co and routine stand for  cooperation and function respectively  a core routine is a coatland feature  that can perform everything a thread can  do  while still be incredibly efficient  a core routine is a lightweight code  that doesn't require any processor  background switching and doesn't map on  native threads  so this is co routines  now let's have a look at the 15th  question which is  difference between safe calls and null  check  safe call operat