stract class  b  it represents this restricted class  hierarchies  c  it is used in every kotlin program  d none of the above  the correct option is option b  it represents restricted class  hierarchies  so  the restricted class hierarchies defines  the seed class in  kotlin now moving on to the 24th  question which is what is lazy  initialization in kotlin so lazy  initialization is a feature in kotlin  that indicates that your variable will  not be initialized unless you utilize it  in your code  if it only be initialized once  after that you repeat the process with  the same value  so now moving on to our 25th question  which is what is the entry point of  every courtling program  every kotlin program's entry point is  the main function  the main function does not have to be  written inside the class in kotlin the  jvm automatically encapsulates it in a  class when it is compiled  the command line arguments are retrieved  using the strings given in the form of  array string  so this was the answer of this question  now moving on to the next question which  is what are companion objects in kotlin  so if we wish to write a function or a  member of a class that may be called  without needing the class instance  we can do so as a member of companion  object within the class in kotlin  as a result by declaring the companion  object we can only access the class  member by class name so this was the  answer of companion objects in kotlin  now moving on to the 27th question  which is  where does this kotlin run  cortland programs can execute on a  normal jvm just like any other compiled  java code  this means that the kotlin compiler  converts cortling programs to bytecode  that the jvm can understand  as a result kotlin is a java kind that  works alongside with java so basically  kotlin is a kind of java you can say  that  it is worth noting that  bits of java code can be used to create  kotlin applications  so now our next question is why do we  need object keyword the